<http://rs.tdwg.org/dwc/terms/Occurrence.rdf> <http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/creator> "Biodiversity Information Standards (TDWG)" .
<http://rs.tdwg.org/dwc/terms/Occurrence.rdf> <http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/format> "application/rdf+xml" .
<http://rs.tdwg.org/dwc/terms/Occurrence.rdf> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/modified> "2026-06-07T12:26:59-03:00"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> .
<http://rs.tdwg.org/dwc/terms/Occurrence.rdf> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/references> <http://rs.tdwg.org/dwc/terms/Occurrence> .
<http://rs.tdwg.org/dwc/terms/Occurrence.rdf> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://xmlns.com/foaf/0.1/document> .
<http://rs.tdwg.org/dwc/terms/Occurrence> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/created> "2009-04-29"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date> .
<http://rs.tdwg.org/dwc/terms/Occurrence> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "In Darwin Core, dwc:Organism, dwc:Occurrence, and dwc:MaterialEntity are related, but distinct concepts. A dwc:Organism is a biological individual or group with an identity and life history that persists independently of the particular dwc:MaterialEntities through which it is manifested. A dwc:Occurrence is a dwc:Event that represents the presence or state of a dwc:Organism at a place during an interval of time, with no explicit dependency on any dwc:MaterialEntity. A dwc:MaterialEntity represents physical matter, including whole bodies, parts, or derivatives of dwc:Organisms, that may directly or indirectly serve as evidence of a dwc:Occurrence."@en .
<http://rs.tdwg.org/dwc/terms/Occurrence> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/hasVersion> <http://rs.tdwg.org/dwc/terms/version/Occurrence-2009-04-29> .
