<http://rs.tdwg.org/dwc/terms/footprintSRS.rdf> <http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/creator> "Biodiversity Information Standards (TDWG)" .
<http://rs.tdwg.org/dwc/terms/footprintSRS.rdf> <http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/format> "application/rdf+xml" .
<http://rs.tdwg.org/dwc/terms/footprintSRS.rdf> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/modified> "2025-07-07T15:53:12-05:00"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> .
<http://rs.tdwg.org/dwc/terms/footprintSRS.rdf> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/references> <http://rs.tdwg.org/dwc/terms/footprintSRS> .
<http://rs.tdwg.org/dwc/terms/footprintSRS.rdf> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://xmlns.com/foaf/0.1/document> .
<http://rs.tdwg.org/dwc/terms/footprintSRS> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/created> "2009-07-06"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date> .
<http://rs.tdwg.org/dwc/terms/footprintSRS> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "Recommended best practice is to use the EPSG code of the SRS, if known. Otherwise use a controlled vocabulary for the name or code of the geodetic datum, if known. Otherwise use a controlled vocabulary for the name or code of the ellipsoid, if known. If none of these is known, use the value `not recorded`. It is also permitted to provide the SRS in Well-Known-Text, especially if no EPSG code provides the necessary values for the attributes of the SRS. Do not use this term to describe the SRS of the dwc:decimalLatitude and dwc:decimalLongitude, nor of any verbatim coordinates - use the dwc:geodeticDatum and dwc:verbatimSRS instead. This term has an equivalent in the dwciri: namespace that allows only an IRI as a value, whereas this term allows for any string literal value."@en .
<http://rs.tdwg.org/dwc/terms/footprintSRS> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/hasVersion> <http://rs.tdwg.org/dwc/terms/version/footprintSRS-2009-07-06> .
<http://rs.tdwg.org/dwc/terms/footprintSRS> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/hasVersion> <http://rs.tdwg.org/dwc/terms/version/footprintSRS-2017-10-06> .
<http://rs.tdwg.org/dwc/terms/footprintSRS> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/hasVersion> <http://rs.tdwg.org/dwc/terms/version/footprintSRS-2018-09-06> .
<http://rs.tdwg.org/dwc/terms/footprintSRS> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/hasVersion> <http://rs.tdwg.org/dwc/terms/version/footprintSRS-2021-07-15> .
<http://rs.tdwg.org/dwc/terms/footprintSRS> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/hasVersion> <http://rs.tdwg.org/dwc/terms/version/footprintSRS-2023-06-28> .
<http://rs.tdwg.org/dwc/terms/footprintSRS> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/hasVersion> <http://rs.tdwg.org/dwc/terms/version/footprintSRS-2025-06-12> .
<http://rs.tdwg.org/dwc/terms/footprintSRS> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/isPartOf> <http://rs.tdwg.org/dwc/terms/> .
<http://rs.tdwg.org/dwc/terms/footprintSRS> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/modified> "2025-06-12"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date> .
<http://rs.tdwg.org/dwc/terms/footprintSRS> <http://rs.tdwg.org/dwc/terms/attributes/abcdEquivalence> "not in ABCD" .
<http://rs.tdwg.org/dwc/terms/footprintSRS> <http://rs.tdwg.org/dwc/terms/attributes/organizedInClass> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/Location> .
<http://rs.tdwg.org/dwc/terms/footprintSRS> <http://rs.tdwg.org/dwc/terms/attributes/usageScope> "simple" .
<http://rs.tdwg.org/dwc/terms/footprintSRS> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#Property> .
<http://rs.tdwg.org/dwc/terms/footprintSRS> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The ellipsoid, geodetic datum, or spatial reference system (SRS) upon which the geometry given in dwc:footprintWKT is based."@en .
<http://rs.tdwg.org/dwc/terms/footprintSRS> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <http://rs.tdwg.org/dwc/terms/> .
<http://rs.tdwg.org/dwc/terms/footprintSRS> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Footprint SRS"@en .
<http://rs.tdwg.org/dwc/terms/footprintSRS> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The ellipsoid, geodetic datum, or spatial reference system (SRS) upon which the geometry given in dwc:footprintWKT is based."@en .
<http://rs.tdwg.org/dwc/terms/footprintSRS> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "`EPSG:4326`; `GEOGCS[\"GCS_WGS_1984\", DATUM[\"D_WGS_1984\", SPHEROID[\"WGS_1984\",6378137,298.257223563]], PRIMEM[\"Greenwich\",0], UNIT[\"Degree\",0.0174532925199433]]` (WKT for the standard WGS84 Spatial Reference System EPSG:4326); `not recorded`"@en .
<http://rs.tdwg.org/dwc/terms/footprintSRS> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "Footprint SRS"@en .
<http://rs.tdwg.org/dwc/terms/footprintSpatialFit.rdf> <http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/creator> "Biodiversity Information Standards (TDWG)" .
<http://rs.tdwg.org/dwc/terms/footprintSpatialFit.rdf> <http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/format> "application/rdf+xml" .
<http://rs.tdwg.org/dwc/terms/footprintSpatialFit.rdf> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/modified> "2026-06-07T12:26:59-03:00"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> .
<http://rs.tdwg.org/dwc/terms/footprintSpatialFit.rdf> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/references> <http://rs.tdwg.org/dwc/terms/footprintSpatialFit> .
<http://rs.tdwg.org/dwc/terms/footprintSpatialFit.rdf> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://xmlns.com/foaf/0.1/document> .
<http://rs.tdwg.org/dwc/terms/footprintSpatialFit> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/created> "2009-04-24"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date> .
<http://rs.tdwg.org/dwc/terms/footprintSpatialFit> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "Legal values are 0, greater than or equal to 1, or undefined. A value of 1 is an exact match or 100% overlap. A value of 0 should be used if the given footprint does not completely contain the original representation. A dwc:footprintSpatialFit is undefined (and should be left empty) if the original representation is any geometry without area (e.g., a point or polyline) and without uncertainty and the given georeference is not that same geometry (without uncertainty). If both the original and the given georeference are the same point, a dwc:footprintSpatialFit is 1. Detailed explanations with graphical examples can be found in the Georeferencing Best Practices, Chapman and Wieczorek, 2020 (https://doi.org/10.15468/doc-gg7h-s853)."@en .
<http://rs.tdwg.org/dwc/terms/footprintSpatialFit> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/hasVersion> <http://rs.tdwg.org/dwc/terms/version/footprintSpatialFit-2009-04-24> .
<http://rs.tdwg.org/dwc/terms/footprintSpatialFit> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/hasVersion> <http://rs.tdwg.org/dwc/terms/version/footprintSpatialFit-2017-10-06> .
<http://rs.tdwg.org/dwc/terms/footprintSpatialFit> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/hasVersion> <http://rs.tdwg.org/dwc/terms/version/footprintSpatialFit-2020-08-20> .
<http://rs.tdwg.org/dwc/terms/footprintSpatialFit> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/hasVersion> <http://rs.tdwg.org/dwc/terms/version/footprintSpatialFit-2023-06-28> .
<http://rs.tdwg.org/dwc/terms/footprintSpatialFit> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/hasVersion> <http://rs.tdwg.org/dwc/terms/version/footprintSpatialFit-2026-05-26> .
<http://rs.tdwg.org/dwc/terms/footprintSpatialFit> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/isPartOf> <http://rs.tdwg.org/dwc/terms/> .
<http://rs.tdwg.org/dwc/terms/footprintSpatialFit> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/modified> "2026-05-26"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date> .
<http://rs.tdwg.org/dwc/terms/footprintSpatialFit> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/replaces> <http://rs.tdwg.org/dwc/geospatial/FootprintSpatialFit> .
<http://rs.tdwg.org/dwc/terms/footprintSpatialFit> <http://rs.tdwg.org/dwc/terms/attributes/abcdEquivalence> "DataSets/DataSet/Units/Unit/Gathering/FootprintSpatialFit" .
<http://rs.tdwg.org/dwc/terms/footprintSpatialFit> <http://rs.tdwg.org/dwc/terms/attributes/organizedInClass> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/Location> .
<http://rs.tdwg.org/dwc/terms/footprintSpatialFit> <http://rs.tdwg.org/dwc/terms/attributes/usageScope> "simple" .
<http://rs.tdwg.org/dwc/terms/footprintSpatialFit> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#Property> .
<http://rs.tdwg.org/dwc/terms/footprintSpatialFit> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A ratio of the area of a footprint (dwc:footprintWKT) to the area of a true (original, or most specific) spatial representation of a dcterms:Location."@en .
