<http://rs.tdwg.org/dwc/terms/verbatimLabel> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/created> "2023-06-28"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date> .
<http://rs.tdwg.org/dwc/terms/verbatimLabel> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "The content of this term should include no embellishments, prefixes, headers or other additions made to the text. Abbreviations must not be expanded and supposed misspellings must not be corrected. Lines or breakpoints between blocks of text that could be verified by seeing the original labels or images of them may be used. Examples of material entities include preserved specimens, fossil specimens, and material samples. Best practice is to use UTF-8 for all characters. Best practice is to add comment “verbatimLabel derived from human transcription” in dwc:materialEntityRemarks. Examples can be found at https://dwc.tdwg.org/examples/verbatimLabel."@en .
<http://rs.tdwg.org/dwc/terms/verbatimLabel> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/hasVersion> <http://rs.tdwg.org/dwc/terms/version/verbatimLabel-2023-06-28> .
<http://rs.tdwg.org/dwc/terms/verbatimLabel> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/hasVersion> <http://rs.tdwg.org/dwc/terms/version/verbatimLabel-2023-09-13> .
<http://rs.tdwg.org/dwc/terms/verbatimLabel> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/hasVersion> <http://rs.tdwg.org/dwc/terms/version/verbatimLabel-2026-05-26> .
